# What the robot works on from now on, as a natural-language prompt, at a GUIDE-EX layer:
#   level "task"    -- one complete job, e.g. "Put the red cube on the blue cube."; it is
#                      every following frame's LeRobot task.
#   level "subtask" -- a part of the task, e.g. "Pick up the red cube."; it is recorded as
#                      LeRobot's `subtask` language style.
# Every frame the scene records after this carries it, until the next prompt of the same
# level or the end of the episode. An empty prompt is not recorded: a level is replaced,
# never cleared (an empty task leaves the frames to the procedure). The procedure-level
# prompt ("Stack the cubes.") is drawn by the scene's randomization and recorded as GUIDE's
# `procedure` language style.
int32 id
string level
string prompt
---
bool success
string message
